所以它不只是往上走
So it's not just going up,

143
00:07:09,720 --> 00:07:10,840
而是越涨越快
it's going up faster and faster.

144
00:07:12,020 --> 00:07:13,340
当我刚开始做Claude Code的时候
When I first started Claude Code,

145
00:07:13,500 --> 00:07:16,860
它本来只是一个小小的黑客式尝试
it was just supposed to be a little hack.

146
00:07:18,480 --> 00:07:23,260
在Anthropic内部，我们大致知道自己想要推出某种编码产品
We broadly knew at Anthropic that we wanted to ship some kind of coding product.

147
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:26,060
而对Anthropic来说，在很长一段时间里
And for Anthropic, for a long time,

148
00:07:26,420 --> 00:07:31,520
我们一直在用一种符合我们构建安全AI心智模型的方式来训练模型
we were building the models in this way that kind of fit our mental model of the way that we built SafeHAI.

149
00:07:31,520 --> 00:07:34,540
在这个路径里，模型一开始要先非常擅长写代码
Where the model starts by being really good at coding,

150
00:07:34,760 --> 00:07:35,940
然后再变得非常擅长工具使用
then it gets really good at tool use,

151
00:07:36,020 --> 00:07:37,340
接着再变得非常擅长计算机使用
then it gets really good at computer use.

152
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:39,100
大致来说，这就是整个演进轨迹
Roughly, this is the trajectory.

153
00:07:40,380 --> 00:07:42,100
而我们在这条路线上已经耕耘了很久
And we've been working on this for a long time.

154
00:07:43,100 --> 00:07:45,860
如果你回头看我最初所在的那个团队
And when you look at the team that I started on,

155
00:07:45,920 --> 00:07:47,160
它叫做Anthropic Labs团队
it was called the Anthropic Labs team.

156
00:07:47,620 --> 00:07:49,380
而且实际上，迈克·克里格和本·曼
And actually, Mike Krieger and Ben Mann,

157
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:52,380
他们刚刚又把这个团队重新启动，相当于第二轮
they just kicked this team off again for kind of round two.

158
00:07:53,020 --> 00:07:54,760
这个团队做出了一些非常酷的东西
The team built some pretty cool stuff.

159
00:07:54,940 --> 00:07:56,040
比如我们做了Claude Code
So we built Claude Code,

160
00:07:56,140 --> 00:07:57,800
我们做了MCP，也做了桌面应用
we built MCP, we built the desktop app.

161
00:07:58,600 --> 00:08:00,280
所以你大概能看到这个想法的种子
So you can kind of see the seeds of this idea.

162
00:08:00,940 --> 00:08:02,380
先是编码，然后是工具使用
It's coding, then it's tool use,

163
00:08:02,460 --> 00:08:03,240
接着是计算机使用
then it's computer use.

164
00:08:04,260 --> 00:08:07,900
而这对Anthropic之所以重要，是因为安全
And the reason this matters for Anthropic is because of safety.

165
00:08:08,200 --> 00:08:11,780
这又回到了那个话题：AI正变得越来越强大
It's kind of, again, just back to that AI is getting more and more powerful.

166
00:08:11,980 --> 00:08:12,960
它的能力越来越强
It's getting more and more capable.

167
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:15,880
在过去一年里发生的一件事是
The thing that's happened in the last year is that,

168
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:17,160
至少对工程师来说
at least for engineers,

169
00:08:17,380 --> 00:08:18,740
AI不再只是写代码
the AI doesn't just write the code.

170
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:20,320
它不再只是一个对话伙伴
It's not just a conversation partner,

171
00:08:20,380 --> 00:08:21,480
而是会真正使用工具
but it actually uses tools.

172
00:08:21,740 --> 00:08:22,680
它会在现实世界中采取行动
It acts in the world.

173
00:08:23,420 --> 00:08:24,680
而我认为，现在有了Claude的计算机使用能力
And I think now with Claude computer use,

174
00:08:24,760 --> 00:08:28,320
我们开始看到这种转变也在发生在非技术人群身上
we're starting to see the transition for non-technical folks also.

175
00:08:29,320 --> 00:08:31,400
对于很多使用对话式AI的人来说
For a lot of people that use conversational AI,

176
00:08:32,120 --> 00:08:34,920
这可能是他们第一次在用一个真正会采取行动的东西
this might be the first time that they're using the thing that actually acts.

177
00:08:35,060 --> 00:08:36,020
它真的可以使用你的Gmail
It can actually use your Gmail,

178
00:08:36,180 --> 00:08:37,000
它可以使用你的Slack
it can use your Slack.

179
00:08:37,460 --> 00:08:38,560
它可以替你完成所有这些事情
You can do all these things for you,

180
00:08:38,580 --> 00:08:39,700
而且做得相当不错
and it's quite good at it.

181
00:08:39,840 --> 00:08:41,320
而且从现在开始它只会变得越来越好
And it's only going to get better from here.

182
00:08:42,480 --> 00:08:43,240
所以我认为对Anthropic来说
So I think for Anthropic,

183
00:08:43,340 --> 00:08:45,720
很长一段时间里，我们都有一种想要构建某种东西的感觉
for a long time, there was this feeling that we wanted to build something,

184
00:08:45,780 --> 00:08:46,780
但并不清楚具体是什么
but it wasn't obvious what.

185
00:08:47,540 --> 00:08:49,380
所以当我加入Anthropic的时候
And so when I joined Anthropic,

186
00:08:49,380 --> 00:08:51,380
我花了一个月时间在做各种hack
I spent one month hacking,

187
00:08:51,720 --> 00:08:54,160
做了一堆古怪的原型，其中大多数都没有发布
and built a bunch of weird prototypes most of them didn't ship,

188
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:56,120
甚至离发布都还差得很远
and weren't even close to shipping.

189
00:08:56,120 --> 00:08:58,820
主要是为了理解模型能力的边界
It was just understanding the boundaries of what the model can do.

190
00:08:59,520 --> 00:09:01,420
然后我又花了一个月做后训练
Then I spent a month doing post-training,

191
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:03,920
以便从研究的角度去理解这一切
so to understand the research side of it.

192
00:09:04,600 --> 00:09:05,320
说实话，我认为
And I think honestly,

193
00:09:05,420 --> 00:09:06,800
这对我作为一个工程师来说
that's just for me as an engineer.

194
00:09:07,380 --> 00:09:09,000
我发现要把工作做好
I find that to do good work,

195
00:09:09,060 --> 00:09:12,380
你必须真正理解你所处那一层之下的那一层
you really have to understand the layer under the layer at which you work.

196
00:09:13,440 --> 00:09:15,080
而在传统工程工作中
And with traditional engineering work,

197
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:16,340
如果你在做一个产品
if you're working on a product,

198
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:17,940
你需要理解底层基础设施
you want to understand the infrastructure,

199
00:09:18,320 --> 00:09:19,780
运行时、虚拟机
the runtime, the virtual machine,

200
00:09:20,260 --> 00:09:21,680
语言本身，不管是什么语言
the language, whatever that is,

201
00:09:21,720 --> 00:09:22,740
以及你所构建其上的整个系统
the system that you're building on.

202
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:25,820
但如果你在做AI相关的工作
But yeah, if you're working in AI,

203
00:09:26,000 --> 00:09:29,320
你就必须在一定程度上真正理解这个模型，才能把工作做好
you just really have to understand the model to some degree to do good work.

204
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:32,180
所以我稍微绕了个路去做这件事
So I took a little detour to do that,

205
00:09:32,240 --> 00:09:35,900
然后我回过头来，开始做原型，做的东西最终就变成了Claude Code
and then I came back and just started prototyping what eventually became Claude Code.

206
00:09:36,860 --> 00:09:38,320
至于它的第一个版本
And the very first version of it,

207
00:09:38,480 --> 00:09:39,580
我这儿有一个那种
I have like a...

208
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:41,020
有一段那个夏天录下来的视频
There's like a video recording of the summer,

209
00:09:41,100 --> 00:09:42,120
因为我录了这个演示
because I recorded this demo,

210
00:09:42,620 --> 00:09:43,540
然后把它发了出去
and I posted it.

211
00:09:43,580 --> 00:09:47,400
那时候它叫做 Claude CLI 然后我就随便展示了一下它是怎么用上几个工具的
It was called Claude CLI back then. And I just kind of showed off how it used a few tools,

212
00:09:47,460 --> 00:09:50,560
让我震惊的是，我给了它一个bash工具
and the shocking thing for me was that I gave it a bash tool,

213
00:09:50,560 --> 00:09:56,540
它就能用那个工具写出代码，告诉我我正在听什么音乐
and it just was able to use that to write code to tell me what music I'm listening to,

214
00:09:56,580 --> 00:09:57,220
当我问它类似
when I asked it, like,

215
00:09:57,300 --> 00:09:58,420
我现在在听什么歌
what music am I listening to?

216
00:09:59,240 --> 00:10:01,220
这简直太疯狂了对吧
And this is the craziest thing, right?

217
00:10:01,260 --> 00:10:05,000
因为我根本没有——我没有告诉模型说
Because it's like, there's no... I didn't instruct the model to say,

218
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:07,600
你要用这个工具来干这件事
you know, use this tool for this,

219
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:08,420
或者该怎么做之类的
or kind of do whatever.

220
00:10:08,560 --> 00:10:09,720
模型只是被提供了这个工具
The model was given this tool,

221
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:12,620
然后它自己想明白了怎么用它来回答我这个问题
and it figured out how to use it to answer this question that I had,

222
00:10:12,640 --> 00:10:13,880
而我当时都不确定它能不能回答
but I wasn't even sure if it could answer,

223
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:15,240
我现在在听什么歌
what music am I listening to?

224
00:10:16,580 --> 00:10:19,900
所以我就继续多做了一些原型
And so I started prototyping this a little bit more,

225
00:10:20,540 --> 00:10:21,740
然后写了一篇帖子
and made a post about it,

226
00:10:21,860 --> 00:10:23,060
在公司内部做了个发布
and I announced it internally,

227
00:10:23,340 --> 00:10:24,160
然后只收获了两个点赞
and it got two likes.

228
00:10:25,220 --> 00:10:28,660
当时的反响大概就是这个水平
That was the sense of the reaction at the time.

229
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:30,380
我觉得是因为公司内部的人
Because I think people internally,

230
00:10:30,580 --> 00:10:31,720
你知道，当你想到编程工具时
you know, like, when you think of coding tools,

231
00:10:31,800 --> 00:10:35,980
你会想到IDE，会想到各种非常复杂的开发环境
you think of IDEs, you think about kind of all these pretty sophisticated environments.

232
00:10:36,700 --> 00:10:39,160
没有人觉得这种东西可以是基于终端的
No one thought that this thing could be terminal-based.

233
00:10:39,820 --> 00:10:41,440
这种设计方式有点怪
That's sort of a weird way to design it,

234
00:10:41,460 --> 00:10:42,520
而且一开始也不是刻意要这么做
and that wasn't really the intention.

235
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:45,040
但你看，从一开始
But, you know, from the start,

236
00:10:45,120 --> 00:10:46,040
我就是在终端里把它做出来的
I built it in a terminal,

237
00:10:46,220 --> 00:10:48,220
因为前几个月
because, you know, for the first couple months,

238
00:10:48,240 --> 00:10:48,820
只有我一个人在做
it was just me.

239
00:10:48,820 --> 00:10:50,840
所以这是最省事的开发方式
So it was just the easiest way to build.

240
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:54,100
对我来说，这其实是一个很重要的产品教训
And for me, this is actually a pretty important product lesson.

241
00:10:54,700 --> 00:10:57,280
就是说，一开始你反而要刻意少投入一点资源
It's like, you want to under-resource things a little bit at the start.

242
00:10:58,480 --> 00:11:02,760
后来我们开始思考还应该做哪些形态
Then we started thinking about what other form factors we should build,

243
00:11:02,840 --> 00:11:05,060
结果我们决定再坚持用终端一段时间
and we actually decided to stick with the terminal for a while.

244
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:09,020
最大的原因是模型进步得太快了
And the biggest reason was the model is improving so quickly.

245
00:11:09,640 --> 00:11:12,920
我们觉得没有别的形态能跟得上它的迭代速度
We felt that there wasn't really another form factor that could keep up with it.

246
00:11:13,440 --> 00:11:16,160
说实话，那时候我自己也在纠结
And honestly, this was just me kind of, like, struggling with,

247
00:11:16,160 --> 00:11:17,600
我们到底该做成什么样
kind of like, what should we build?

248
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:18,740
你想，在过去这一年里
You know, like, for the last year,

249
00:11:18,900 --> 00:11:20,440
Claude Code几乎是我脑子里唯一在想的东西
the Claude Code has just been all I think about.

250
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:22,220
所以在深夜的时候
And so just, like, late at night,

251
00:11:22,300 --> 00:11:23,600
我脑子里想的就是这些事
this is just something I was thinking about.

252
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:25,260
比如说，好，模型还在不断变强
Like, okay, the model's continuing to improve.

253
00:11:25,760 --> 00:11:27,240
我们该怎么办 我们怎么可能跟得上
What do we do? How can we possibly keep up?

254
00:11:27,600 --> 00:11:29,960
说实话，终端就是我唯一能想到的办法
And the terminal was honestly just the only idea that I had.

255
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:33,220
然后它最后真的火起来了
And, yeah, it ended up catching on.

256
00:11:33,640 --> 00:11:36,280
在我发布之后没多久
After I released it pretty quickly,

257
00:11:36,700 --> 00:11:38,080
它就在Anthropic内部大受欢迎
it became a hit at Anthropic,

258
00:11:38,280 --> 00:11:40,840
日活跃用户直接垂直起飞
and, you know, the daily active users just went vertical.

259
00:11:41,020 --> 00:11:42,160
其实在很早的时候
And really early on, actually,

260
00:11:42,200 --> 00:11:42,900
在我正式发布之前
before I launched it,

261
00:11:42,940 --> 00:11:45,900
本·曼就提醒我做一张日活曲线图
Ben Mann nudged me to make a DAU chart.

262
00:11:46,160 --> 00:11:47,000
当时我还在想
And I was like, you know,

263
00:11:47,060 --> 00:11:47,700
现在做这个有点太早了吧
it's kind of early.

264
00:11:47,820 --> 00:11:49,600
要不要现在就做呢
Maybe, you know, should we really do it right now?

265
00:11:49,660 --> 00:11:50,200
而他的回答是，要做
And he was like, yeah.

266
00:11:51,180 --> 00:11:53,400
结果那张图几乎立刻就变成了一条竖线
And so the chart just went vertical pretty immediately.

267
00:11:53,840 --> 00:11:55,580
然后到了二月份
And then in February,

268
00:11:55,600 --> 00:11:56,780
我们把它对外发布了
we released it externally.

269
00:11:57,600 --> 00:12:00,180
其实有件事大家现在不太记得了
Actually, something that people don't really remember is,

270
00:12:00,460 --> 00:12:03,880
Claude Code刚发布的时候并不算爆款
Claude Code was not initially a hit when we released it.

271
00:12:03,980 --> 00:12:05,100
它确实获得了一批用户
It got a bunch of users.

272
00:12:05,560 --> 00:12:07,620
有很多早期用户立刻就上手了
There was a lot of early adopters that got it immediately.

273
00:12:08,120 --> 00:12:11,940
但大家真正搞明白这到底是什么东西，花了好几个月
But it actually took many months for everyone to really understand what this thing is.

274
00:12:12,520 --> 00:12:14,240
因为再说一遍，它实在太不一样了
Just, again, it's just so different.

275
00:12:14,940 --> 00:12:16,380
回过头来看
And when I think about it,

276
00:12:16,680 --> 00:12:19,820
Claude Code之所以有效，部分原因是存在一种“潜在需求”
kind of part of the reason Claude Code works is this idea of latent demand,

277
00:12:20,520 --> 00:12:22,520
我们把工具带到人们本来就在的地方
where we bring the tool to where people are,

278
00:12:22,640 --> 00:12:24,400
让他们现有的工作流变得稍微轻松一点
and it makes existing workflows a little bit easier.

279
00:12:24,960 --> 00:12:26,640
但也因为它是在终端里
But also because it's in a terminal,

280
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:27,520
所以会有点出乎意料
it's like a little surprising.

281
00:12:27,660 --> 00:12:28,760
在某种意义上有点“外星”
It's a little alien in this way.

282
00:12:28,840 --> 00:12:30,820
所以你得稍微保持开放一点
So you have to kind of be open-minded,

283
00:12:30,940 --> 00:12:32,380
也得花点时间学着用它
and you have to learn to use it.

284
00:12:33,060 --> 00:12:35,300
当然，现在Claude Code已经可以在很多地方用了
And, of course, now, you know, Claude Code is available,

285
00:12:35,560 --> 00:12:37,540
比如iOS和Android上的Claude应用里
you know, in the iOS and Android Claude app.

286
00:12:37,840 --> 00:12:39,400
桌面应用里也有
It's available in the desktop app.

287
00:12:39,420 --> 00:12:40,360
网站上也能用
It's available on the website.

288
00:12:40,560 --> 00:12:43,620
还可以作为IDE扩展，在Slack和GitHub里使用
It's available as IDE extensions in Slack and GitHub.

289
00:12:43,620 --> 00:12:45,440
也就是工程师们本来就在的那些地方
You know, all of these places where engineers are,

290
00:12:45,580 --> 00:12:46,320
这样就会更熟悉一些
it's a little more familiar.

291
00:12:46,880 --> 00:12:47,900
但一开始并不是这样
But that wasn't the starting point.

292
00:12:49,300 --> 00:12:51,460
所以说，在最初的时候
So, yeah, I mean, at the beginning,

293
00:12:51,560 --> 00:12:54,040
这玩意儿居然真的有用，这点本身就挺让人意外的
it was kind of a surprise that this thing was even useful.

294
00:12:55,800 --> 00:12:57,440
然后随着团队壮大
And, you know, as the team grew,

295
00:12:57,580 --> 00:13:01,640
随着产品成长，随着它对越来越多的人变得真正有用
as the product grew, as it started to become more and more useful to people,

296
00:13:02,180 --> 00:13:03,580
就是来自世界各地的人，从
just people around the world from,

297
00:13:03,680 --> 00:13:06,480
你知道的，小型初创公司到最大的FANG公司都开始使用它
you know, small startups to the biggest fang companies started using it.

298
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:08,240
然后他们开始给我们反馈
And they started giving feedback.

299
00:13:09,280 --> 00:13:10,940
回过头来看
And I think just reflecting back,

300
00:13:11,060 --> 00:13:12,740
这真是一次让人非常谦卑的经历
it's been such a humbling experience.

301
00:13:12,740 --> 00:13:15,060
因为我们一直在向用户学习
Because we just, we keep learning from our users.

302
00:13:15,440 --> 00:13:17,420
而最让人兴奋的是
And just the most exciting thing is,

303
00:13:17,600 --> 00:13:19,200
你知道，其实我们谁都不是真的完全知道自己在做什么
like, you know, none of us really know what we're doing.

304
00:13:20,020 --> 00:13:22,460
