00:45:37,410 --> 00:45:39,430
是的 我在一些地方也有类似的观察
Yeah, I'm seeing this a little bit with...

1068
00:45:39,430 --> 00:45:42,670
在Anthropic 我觉得每个人都相当偏技术
At Anthropic, I think everyone is fairly technical.

1069
00:45:43,710 --> 00:45:45,190
这是我们在筛选时会看重的一点
This is something that we screen for,

1070
00:45:45,310 --> 00:45:46,470
也就是人们加入公司时
you know, when people join.

1071
00:45:46,590 --> 00:45:49,770
我们会有 很多技术面试环节需要候选人通过
We have... there's a lot of technical interviews that people go through,

1072
00:45:49,990 --> 00:45:51,670
即便是非技术岗位也是如此
even for non-technical functions.

1073
00:45:53,330 --> 00:45:56,690
而且你知道 我们的设计师大多也会写代码
And, you know, our designers largely code.

1074
00:45:57,270 --> 00:46:02,310
所以从我看到的情况来看 对他们来说这是他们很享受的一件事
So I think for them, this is something that they have enjoyed from what I've seen,

1075
00:46:02,430 --> 00:46:04,670
因为现在他们不用再去烦工程师
because now, instead of bugging engineers,

1076
00:46:04,750 --> 00:46:05,970
他们可以自己进去写代码
they can just like go in and code.

1077
00:46:06,430 --> 00:46:09,310
甚至有些之前不会写代码的设计师也开始写了
And even some designers that didn't code before have just started to do it.

1078
00:46:09,610 --> 00:46:11,610
对他们来说这很棒 因为他们可以自己解锁进度
And for them, it's great because they can unblock themselves.

1079
00:46:12,310 --> 00:46:15,150
但我真的很想听到更多人的体验
But I'd be really interested just to hear more people's experiences,

1080
00:46:15,410 --> 00:46:17,490
因为我敢说情况肯定不是这么一致
because I bet it's not uniform like that.

1081
00:46:18,130 --> 00:46:19,290
是的 所以如果你正在听这期节目
Yeah, so maybe if you're listening to this,

1082
00:46:19,410 --> 00:46:22,230
如果你觉得自己的工作变得没那么有趣 更不享受了 可以留言
leave a comment if you're finding your jobs less fun and you're enjoying your job less,

1083
00:46:22,310 --> 00:46:24,870
因为你刚才说的以及我从大多数人那里听到的是
because what you're saying and what I'm hearing from most people,

1084
00:46:24,970 --> 00:46:28,550
有70%的产品经理和工程师更爱自己的工作
70% of PMs and engineers are loving their job more.

1085
00:46:29,030 --> 00:46:30,270
这就意味着 如果你不在那一组里
That's... like, if you're not in that bucket,

1086
00:46:30,550 --> 00:46:32,170
你可以……说明有点不对劲
you could... something's going on.

1087
00:46:32,710 --> 00:46:35,610
对，对 我们确实看到人们也会使用不同的工具
Yeah, yeah. We do see that people use also different tools.

1088
00:46:35,710 --> 00:46:36,870
比如说 我们的设计师们
So, for example, our designers,

1089
00:46:36,870 --> 00:46:40,350
他们更多是用 Claude 桌面应用来写代码
they use the Claude desktop app a lot more to do their coding.

1090
00:46:40,830 --> 00:46:42,130
所以你只要下载这个桌面应用
So you just download the desktop app.

1091
00:46:42,250 --> 00:46:43,030
里面有一个代码标签页
There's a code tab.

1092
00:46:43,610 --> 00:46:45,210
就在 Claude 计算机使用旁边
It's right next to Claude computer use.

1093
00:46:45,210 --> 00:46:46,770
而且它其实就是同一个 Claude Code
And it's actually the same exact Claude Code.

1094
00:46:46,890 --> 00:46:48,270
也就是说是同一个智能体和一切相同的东西
So it's like the same agent and everything.

1095
00:46:48,430 --> 00:46:50,170
这个功能我们已经有很多很多个月了
We've had this for many, many months.

1096
00:46:51,030 --> 00:46:54,470
所以你可以用它来写代码 而不需要打开一堆终端
And so you can use this to code in a way that you don't have to open a bunch of terminals,

1097
00:46:55,210 --> 00:46:57,830
但你依然能获得 Claude Code 的强大能力
but you still get the power of Claude Code.

1098
00:46:57,910 --> 00:47:01,490
而最重要的一点是 你可以并行运行任意多的 Claude 会话
And the biggest thing is you can just run as many Claude sessions in parallel as you want.

1099
00:47:01,970 --> 00:47:03,330
我们 把这个叫作 multi-Claude-ing
We can, you know, we call this multi-Claude-ing.

1100
00:47:03,910 --> 00:47:06,410
所以这算是一个 对他们来说更原生一点的方式
So this is a... it's a little more native,

1101
00:47:06,590 --> 00:47:08,210
我觉得 对那些不是工程师的人来说是这样
I think, for folks that are not engineers.

1102
00:47:08,850 --> 00:47:12,190
归根结底 这就是把产品带到用户所在的场景里
And really, this is back to bringing the product to where the people are.

1103
00:47:12,610 --> 00:47:14,250
你不想强迫人们使用一套完全不同的工作流
You don't want to make people use a different workflow.

1104
00:47:14,470 --> 00:47:16,690
你不想让他们费很大劲去学一个新东西
You don't want to make them go out of their way to learn a new thing.

1105
00:47:17,130 --> 00:47:18,110
不管人们现在在做什么
It's whatever people are doing.

1106
00:47:18,230 --> 00:47:19,590
如果你能让那件事变得稍微容易一点
If you can make that a little bit easier,

1107
00:47:20,190 --> 00:47:23,190
那这个产品就会好得多 人们也会更喜欢
then that's just going to be a much better product that people enjoy more.

1108
00:47:23,770 --> 00:47:25,870
而这就是潜在需求这个原则
And this is just this principle of latent demand,

1109
00:47:25,970 --> 00:47:29,230
我认为这是产品领域里最重要的一个原则
which I think is just the single most important principle in product.

1110
00:47:29,570 --> 00:47:30,750
你能具体讲讲这个吗
Can you talk about that actually?

1111
00:47:30,870 --> 00:47:31,630
因为我正打算聊到这点
Because I was going to go there.

1112
00:47:31,750 --> 00:47:36,950
解释一下这个原则是什么 以及当你释放这种潜在需求时会发生什么
Explain what this principle is and just what happens when you unlock this latent demand.

1113
00:47:37,650 --> 00:47:42,970
潜在需求这个概念是说 如果你把产品做成一种可以被人“黑”一下 或者
Latent demand is this idea that if you build a product in a way that can be hacked or can

1114
00:47:42,970 --> 00:47:46,950
被人以一种最初并非为此设计的方式“误用”
be kind of misused by people in a way it wasn't really designed for,

1115
00:47:47,010 --> 00:47:48,810
用来做他们自己想做的某件事
to do kind of something that they want to do,

1116
00:47:49,870 --> 00:47:54,310
那么这就能帮助你作为产品构建者 学到下一步该把产品带向哪里
then this helps you as the product builder learn where to take the product next.

1117
00:47:55,110 --> 00:47:57,790
一个例子就是 Facebook Marketplace
So an example of this is Facebook Marketplace.

1118
00:47:58,550 --> 00:48:00,010
这个团队的负责人
So the manager for the team,

1119
00:48:00,270 --> 00:48:03,910
Fiona 她其实是 Marketplace 团队的创始负责人
Fiona, she was actually the founding manager for the Marketplace team,

1120
00:48:03,950 --> 00:48:05,170
她经常谈起这件事
and she talks about this a lot.

1121
00:48:06,610 --> 00:48:09,270
Facebook Marketplace 的起点是一个当时的观察
Facebook Marketplace, it started based on the observation back in,

1122
00:48:09,430 --> 00:48:13,110
大概是在 2016 年左右
this must have been like 2016 or something like this,

1123
00:48:13,530 --> 00:48:16,470
发现 Facebook 群组里有 40% 的帖子是在买卖东西
that 40% of posts in Facebook groups are buying and selling stuff.

1124
00:48:17,450 --> 00:48:18,310
这太夸张了
So this is crazy.

1125
00:48:18,470 --> 00:48:21,310
就好像人们在“滥用” Facebook 群组这个产品来买卖东西
It's like people are abusing the Facebook Groups product to buy and sell,

1126
00:48:21,310 --> 00:48:23,670
这里的“滥用”不是安全意义上的那种滥用
and it's not abuse in kind of like a security sense.

1127
00:48:23,770 --> 00:48:26,210
而是说没人一开始是为这个目的设计这个产品的
It's abuse in that no one designed the product for this,

1128
00:48:26,310 --> 00:48:28,870
但大家自己摸索出来 因为拿它来做这件事实在太好用了
but they're kind of figuring it out because it's just so useful for this.

1129
00:48:29,990 --> 00:48:33,130
所以很明显 如果你做一个更好的产品 让人们买卖东西
And so it was pretty obvious if you build a better product to let people buy and sell,

1130
00:48:33,250 --> 00:48:33,970
他们一定会喜欢
they're going to like it.

1131
00:48:34,310 --> 00:48:37,510
从这一点看 Marketplace 会火几乎是显而易见的
And it was just very obvious that Marketplace would be a hit from this.

1132
00:48:37,590 --> 00:48:39,350
所以第一步是“买卖群组”
And so the first thing was buy and sell groups,

1133
00:48:39,410 --> 00:48:42,310
也就是专门为买卖设计的群组
so kind of special purpose groups to let people do that.

1134
00:48:42,370 --> 00:48:43,950
第二个产品才是 Marketplace
And the second product was Marketplace.

1135
00:48:45,550 --> 00:48:46,670
我觉得 Facebook 交友也是类似
Facebook dating, I think,

1136
00:48:46,730 --> 00:48:48,130
它的起点也差不多
started in a pretty similar place.

1137
00:48:48,750 --> 00:48:52,770
当时的观察是 如果你看人们在看什么 如果你看
And I think that the observation was if you look at people looking at... if you look at

1138
00:48:52,770 --> 00:48:55,590
个人资料浏览量 也就是人们在 Facebook 上互相看对方的主页
profile views, so people looking at each other's profiles on Facebook,

1139
00:48:56,130 --> 00:48:59,010
有 60% 的资料浏览发生在互相不是好友的人之间
60% of profile views are people that are not friends with each other,

1140
00:48:59,090 --> 00:48:59,850
而且还是异性之间
that are opposite gender.

1141
00:49:00,950 --> 00:49:02,150
所以这就有点像
And so this is this kind of like,

1142
00:49:02,190 --> 00:49:04,430
你知道 就是传统那种约会场景的设置
you know, like traditional kind of dating set up,

1143
00:49:04,590 --> 00:49:06,290
只是大家在那儿互相“暗中观察”
but, you know, people are just like creeping on each other.

1144
00:49:06,750 --> 00:49:08,290
那如果你能为这种行为做一个产品
So maybe if you can build a product for this,

1145
00:49:08,390 --> 00:49:09,690
可能就会很奏效
it's, you know, it might work.

1146
00:49:11,210 --> 00:49:13,450
所以说 潜在需求这个理念
And so this idea of latent demand,

1147
00:49:13,530 --> 00:49:14,890
我觉得是非常有力量的
I think, is just so powerful.

1148
00:49:16,050 --> 00:49:18,370
比如说 Claude 计算机使用 也是这样来的
And for example, this is also where Claude computer use came from.

1149
00:49:18,910 --> 00:49:21,130
我们发现 在过去大概六个月里
We saw that for the last six months or so,

1150
00:49:21,490 --> 00:49:24,130
许多使用 Claude Code 的人根本不是在写代码
a lot of people using Claude Code were not using it to code.

1151
00:49:24,490 --> 00:49:27,570
有个人在 Twitter 上用它来种番茄
There was someone on Twitter that was using it to grow tomato plants.

1152
00:49:27,670 --> 00:49:29,550
还有人用它来分析自己的基因组
There was someone else using it to analyze their genome.

1153
00:49:30,150 --> 00:49:33,730
有人用它从损坏的硬盘里恢复照片
Someone was using it to recover photos from a corrupted hard drive.

1154
00:49:33,810 --> 00:49:35,310
好像是婚礼照片之类的
It was like wedding photos.

1155
00:49:36,350 --> 00:49:40,610
还有个人在用它做 我记得是那种
There was someone that was using it for, I think, like...

1156
00:49:40,610 --> 00:49:42,610
他们在用它分析核磁共振影像
they were using it to analyze an MRI.

1157
00:49:43,450 --> 00:49:46,510
所以有一大堆完全不算技术性的用例
So there's just all these different use cases that are not technical at all.

1158
00:49:47,150 --> 00:49:48,590
而且非常明显
And it was just really obvious,

1159
00:49:48,790 --> 00:49:52,850
人们在费尽周折地用终端来做这些事
like people are jumping through hoops to use a terminal to do this thing.

1160
00:49:53,330 --> 00:49:54,750
那我们是不是干脆给他们做一个专门的产品
Maybe we should just build a product for them.

1161
00:49:55,250 --> 00:49:56,770
而且我们其实很早就看到了这个趋势
And we saw this actually pretty early,

1162
00:49:57,110 --> 00:49:59,090
大概是去年的五月
back in maybe May of last year.

1163
00:49:59,490 --> 00:50:01,470
我记得我走进办公室 看到我们的数据科学家
I remember walking into the office and our data scientist,

1164
00:50:01,570 --> 00:50:05,270
Brendan 在他的电脑上跑着一个 Claude Code
Brendan, had a Claude Code on his computer.

1165
00:50:05,390 --> 00:50:06,370
他就开着一个终端
He just had a terminal up.

1166
00:50:07,030 --> 00:50:08,510
我当时就震惊了
And I was like, I was shocked.

1167
00:50:09,190 --> 00:50:10,670
我说 Brendan 你在干嘛
I was like, Brendan, what are you doing?

1168
00:50:10,830 --> 00:50:12,690
你居然搞明白了怎么打开终端
Like you figured out how to open the terminal,

1169
00:50:12,830 --> 00:50:15,390
你知道 终端是一个非常工程师向的东西
which is, you know, it's a very engineering product.

1170
00:50:15,470 --> 00:50:17,130
甚至很多工程师都不想用终端
Even a lot of engineers don't want to use a terminal.

1171
00:50:17,270 --> 00:50:21,630
它几乎是做事最底层的那种方式
It's just like the lowest level way to do your work.

1172
00:50:22,350 --> 00:50:25,410
完全是在和计算机的底层细节打交道
Just really, really kind of in the weeds of the computer.

1173
00:50:26,250 --> 00:50:27,610
结果他居然搞懂了怎么用终端
And so he figured out how to use the terminal.

1174
00:50:27,810 --> 00:50:29,930
他下载了 Node.js 又下载了 Claude Code
He downloaded Node.js. He downloaded Claude Code.

1175
00:50:30,490 --> 00:50:32,330
然后在终端里做 SQL 分析
And he was doing SQL analysis in the terminal.

1176
00:50:32,550 --> 00:50:33,830
太夸张了 然后到了下周
It was crazy. And then the next week,

1177
00:50:33,890 --> 00:50:35,490
所有数据科学家都在干同样的事
all the data scientists were doing the same thing.

1178
00:50:36,210 --> 00:50:38,750
所以当你看到人们以这种方式“滥用”产品时
So when you see people abusing the product in this way,

1179
00:50:38,830 --> 00:50:41,950
他们用一种产品本来没为之设计的方式 去做对自己有用的事情
using it in a way that it wasn't designed in order to do something that is useful for

1180
00:50:41,950 --> 00:50:46,830
这就是一个极强的信号 提示你应该为此专门做一个产品
them, it's just such a strong indicator that you should just build a product.

1181
00:50:47,030 --> 00:50:48,170
而人们会喜欢这个新产品
And people are going to like that.

1182
00:50:48,470 --> 00:50:49,870
因为它是为这个用途量身定制的
There's something that's special purpose for that.

1183
00:50:50,550 --> 00:50:53,890
我觉得现在潜在需求还有一个很有意思的第二个维度
I think now there's also this kind of interesting second dimension to latent demand.

1184
00:50:53,990 --> 00:50:57,190
传统的说法是 先看人们在做什么
This is sort of the traditional framing is look at what people are doing,

1185
00:50:57,290 --> 00:50:59,030
然后让那件事变得更容易一点 赋能给他们
make that a little bit easier, empower them.

1186
00:50:59,830 --> 00:51:03,290
我在过去六个月里看到的那种现代化表述方式有点不一样
The modern framing that I've been seeing in the last six months is a little bit different.

1187
00:51:03,470 --> 00:51:09,230
也就是去观察模型想要做什么，然后让它做这些事变得稍微容易一点
And it's look at what the model is trying to do and make that a little bit easier.

1188
00:51:10,390 --> 00:51:12,490
所以当我们一开始构建 Claude Code 的时候
And so when we first started building Claude Code,

1189
00:51:12,570 --> 00:51:17,830
我觉得当时很多人用大模型来设计东西的方式有点像是
I think a lot of the way that people approached designing things with LLMs is they kind of

1190
00:51:17,830 --> 00:51:18,770
把模型关在一个盒子里
put the model in a box.

1191
00:51:19,130 --> 00:51:21,130
他们会说，这是我想要构建的这个应用
And they were here's this application that I want to build.

1192
00:51:21,310 --> 00:51:22,610
这是我想让模型做的那件事
Here's the thing that I wanted to do a model.

1193
00:51:22,750 --> 00:51:24,170
你只负责其中这个组件
You're going to do this one component of it.

1194
00:51:24,330 --> 00:51:27,070
这是你要如何跟这些工具和 API 等等进行交互的方式
Here's the way that you're going to interact with these tools and APIs and whatever.

1195
00:51:27,790 --> 00:51:29,230
而在 Claude Code 上，我们把这一切反过来了
And for Claude Code, we inverted that.

1196
00:51:29,510 --> 00:51:30,810
我们说，产品就是模型本身
We said the product is the model.

1197
00:51:31,130 --> 00:51:32,170
我们想把它尽量暴露出来
We want to expose it.

1198
00:51:32,250 --> 00:51:34,210
我们只想在它周围搭最少的脚手架
We want to put the minimal scaffolding around it.

1199
00:51:34,250 --> 00:51:36,950
给它最少的一组工具，让它自己去完成事情
Give it the minimal set of tools so it can do the things.

1200
00:51:36,990 --> 00:51:38,110
它可以自己决定要运行哪些工具
It can decide which tools to run.

1201
00:51:38,170 --> 00:51:40,670
它可以自己决定运行它们的顺序等等
It can decide what order to run them and so on.

1202
00:51:41,490 --> 00:51:45,210
而我认为很多做法其实是基于模型自身想要做什么这种潜在需求
And I think a lot of this was just based on kind of latent demand of what the model wanted to do.

1203
00:51:45,750 --> 00:51:47,930
在研究里，我们把这叫作“在分布上”
And so in research, we call this being on distribution.

1204
00:51:48,650 --> 00:51:51,170
你想从产品的角度去看模型到底在尝试做什么
You want to see what the model is trying to do in product terms.

1205
00:51:51,630 --> 00:51:54,450
潜在需求其实就是同一个概念，只不过是应用在模型身上
Latent demand is just the same exact concept but applied to a model.

1206
00:51:55,330 --> 00:51:56,190
你刚才提到了 Claude 的计算机使用
You talked about Claude computer use.

1207
00:51:56,330 --> 00:51:59,790
我看到你在最初发布它时提到的一件事是，你们团队
Something that I saw you talk about when you launched that initially is your team built

1208
00:51:59,790 --> 00:52:00,570
用 10 天就把它做出来了
that in 10 days.

1209
00:52:01,370 --> 00:52:03,510
这太疯狂了，它一发布
That's insane. It came out.

1210
00:52:03,550 --> 00:52:06,410
我记得很快就有上百万人在用
I think it was used by millions of people pretty quickly.

1211
00:52:06,870 --> 00:52:08,630
这样的东西在 10 天内就被做出来
